<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;</font></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">When two Agilent LC instr=
uments with VWD are running sequences on one Workstation or AIC, the sequen=
ce aborts after 55 minutes of runtime on one of the LC instruments.</font><=
/pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">With multiple instruments=
 starting at about the same time, longer run times, sequence or single runs=
 may abort with the error =E2=80=9CStore must be open for this operation=E2=
=80=9D in the Activity Log. For example, with an Agilent VWD detector or 12=
20  LC Compact System, a run time of 55 minutes or higher can cause this co=
ndition.
This error occurs due to a Microsoft .NET issue with multiple program threa=
ds writing to a temporary Windows file where the signal size exceeds 10MB. =
For the VWD or 1220 in particular, the reference and sample intensity instr=
ument traces store enough data to exceed this size in about 55 minutes.
This issue only occurs when more than one instrument will exceed the requir=
ed signal size. For example, if using one instrument with a VWD detector an=
d one with PDA, the PDA may not generate the required signal size and the i=
ssue will not occur.
</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This is resolved in OpenL=
AB CDS v2.1 SR1, and OpenLAB CDS v2.2.</font></pre><p></p>




