</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Restarting services fails=
 during Restore on systems with Sample Scheduler activated</font></pre><p><=
/p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">On systems where Sample S=
cheduler is activated, system services can fail to restart during the Resto=
re of a backup, using the OpenLab Backup &amp; Restore utility.=20

The Restore progress dialog will then show a failure in the step where serv=
ices are supposed to start after databases have been restored. </font></pre=
><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">The following workaround =
is available if this problem occurs during a restore on a system where Samp=
le Scheduler application is activated:=20

An entitled user needs to update the name of the service "Agilent Sample Sc=
heduler LIMS Agent" in the backup.xml, in the backup folder.

For a full backup:
in the backup folder "...\Current\backup.xml", change &lt;string&gt;Agilent=
 Sample scheduler LIMS Agent&lt;/string&gt; to &lt;string&gt;Agilent Sample=
 Scheduler LIMS Agent&lt;/string&gt;

For a scheduled backup:
in the backup folder in "...\Current\backup.xml" and in "...\Incremental\ba=
ckup.xml"
change &lt;string&gt;Agilent Sample scheduler LIMS Agent&lt;/string&gt; to =
&lt;string&gt;Agilent Sample Scheduler LIMS Agent&lt;/string&gt;</font></pr=
e><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">The issue has been resolv=
ed in OpenLab CDS 2.8 Update 03 and OpenLab Server 2.8 Update 03.</font></p=
re><p></p>




