<a id=3D"#TTID:" 1156147=3D"" name=3D"TTID:1156147"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:1156147&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CDS 2.8</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;</font></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">No distinction made betwe=
en full- and half-width characters when using Microsoft SQL Server</font></=
pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Secure Storage fails to d=
istinguish between one-byte alphanumeric characters (e.g., =E2=80=9C1=E2=80=
=9D) and two-byte Japanese characters (e.g., =E2=80=9C=EF=BC=91=E2=80=9D) i=
n folder and file names. As a result, folders named =E2=80=9Ctest1=E2=80=9D=
 and =E2=80=9Ctest=EF=BC=91=E2=80=9D are recognized as the same, preventing=
 them from coexisting in the same directory. The error message displayed is=
: =E2=80=9CThis folder name already exists in this location.=E2=80=9D=20

When upgrading systems to v2.8 that already have files/folders in the same =
location that are only distinguished through the use of one-byte vs. two-by=
te characters, the Agilent OpenLab Database Import /Transfer Service applic=
ation will fail on the Data Transformation step with an error similar to: "=
[ERR] Error occurred in WriteNodesToDbAsync. Error Message: Cannot insert d=
uplicate key row in object 'versionedfilestore.nodes' with unique index 'UK=
_nodes'."</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue has been fixed=
 in the newly released installation media, OpenLab ECM XT with Update 4, pu=
blished on SubscribeNet on January 21, 2025.</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
<a id=3D"#TTID:" 1156705=3D"" name=3D"TTID:1156705"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:1156705&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ECM XT 2.8</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;</font></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">OpenSearch Installations =
may fail in case Certificate Revocation List (CRL)  cannot be downloaded</f=
ont></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">On a server which is shie=
lded from the internet the installation of OpenLab Server may fail at the O=
penSearch Configuration step.
The  Agilent_OpenLab_Server_&lt;date&gt;_OpenSearchPackage.log  logfile con=
tains a message like:
System.Exception: Creation of prometheus user failed
   at Agilent.OpenLab.OpenSearch.CustomActions.CustomActions.CreatePromethe=
usUser(Session session) (CustomActions)
CustomAction CaCreatePrometheusUser returned actual error code 1603 (note t=
his may not be 100% accurate if translation happened inside sandbox)

This error is caused by a time-out when attempting downloading a latest ver=
sion of the Certificate Revocation List (CRL).</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">As this issue potential a=
ffects software performance as well as other vendor's software installation=
s, the setup of the  internal Certification Authority (CA) needs to be inve=
stigated.  A Certificate Revocation List Distribution Point for Your Intern=
al Certification Authority should be considered.

To avoid the installation failure it could be considered to disable the CRL=
 update temporarily.  The procedure is described in the Workstation Plus in=
stallation guides.

Further information can also be found in Service Note D0127628 and https://=
learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/networking/technologies/nps/networ=
k-policy-server-certificate-revocation-list-check-registry-settings.

It has been observed the enabling all options (IgnoreNoRevocationCheck, Ign=
oreRevocationOffline, NoRevocationCheck &amp; NoRootRevocationCheck) allowe=
d successful installation of OpenLab Server.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
