p;&nbsp;CDS 2.7 Update 10,ECM XT 2.7 Update 10</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;</font></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Data Repository database =
partially unavailable after installing 2.7 Update 10</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">As part of OpenLab Server=
 2.7 Update 10, a new minor version (14.15) of PostgreSQL 14 gets installed=
. This minor version fixes several security vulnerabilities. During this Po=
stgreSQL update installation, the server certificates associated with the P=
ostgreSQL database are reverted to the default PostgreSQL certificates. As =
a result, specific server-hosted OpenLab services can no longer communicate=
 with the Data Repository database. The impacted client applications are  C=
ary UV and MassHunter Networked Workstations.=20

OpenLab Server/ECM XT v2.7 systems with any of the following software appli=
cations are affected:
- Cary UV Networked Workstation
- LC/MS TQ Acquisition MassHunter Networked Workstation
- GC/MS TQ Acquisition MassHunter Networked Workstation
- MassHunter Quantitative Analysis
- LC/MS Q\TOF Acquisition MassHunter Networked Workstation
- MassHunter Bioconfirm</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is fixed in Op=
enLab Server 2.7 Update 11 and OpenLab CDS 2.7 Update 11. </font></pre><p><=
/p>




<hr>
<a id=3D"#TTID:" 1219719=3D"" name=3D"TTID:1219719"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:1219719&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&n=
bsp;&nbsp;Installer&nbsp;&nbsp;CDS 2.8 Update 06</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;</font></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Backup and Restore utilit=
ies uninstalled during OpenLab CDS 2.8 or OpenLab Server 2.8 software updat=
e</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Installing a software upd=
ate on systems with OpenLab CDS 2.8 Update 05 or OpenLab Server 2.8 Update =
05 will uninstall the Backup and Restore Utilities.

This only affects OpenLab CDS 2.8 Workstations, OpenLab CDS 2.8 Workstation=
 Plus systems, and OpenLab Server/ECM XT 2.8 with Update 05. Upgrading syst=
ems without Update 05 is working as expected.

</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Backup and Restore utilit=
ies can manually be installed by going to Setup\Packages folder in the Soft=
ware Update media and run BackupTool.msi and RestoreTool.msi from their res=
pective folders (Setup\Packages\OpenLab Backup Utility\ and Setup\Packages\=
OpenLab Restore Utility\)</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is fixed in Op=
enLab CDS 2.8 Update 08 with Feature Pack 02 and OpenLab Server 2.8 Update =
08. Please note that installing Update 08 will not reinstall the Backup and=
 Restore Utilities if they had previously been uninstalled. Refer to the Te=
mporary Solution for instructions on how to reinstall the Backup and Restor=
e Utilities.</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
<a id=3D"#TTID:" 1221034=3D"" name=3D"TTID:1221034"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:1221034&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbs=
p;&nbsp;3.1.5</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;</font></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">MBFC signals do not colle=
ct if a No Injection blank is run</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">When "No Injection/Instru=
ment Blank" is selected as the Injection Source when running a Mass-Based F=
raction Collection (MBFC) injection, no data will be collected on the MBFC-=
specific signals (for example, MS1A, MS1B, etc.).  All other signals will b=
e collected as defined in the method.  The MBFC signals cannot be displayed=
, printed, or used for tasks such as blank subtraction or noise calculation=
.

In addition, if a report is generated, it may display "No data available" o=
n the graphical representations of the Sampler's sample container and Fract=
ion Collector's sample container for this "No Injection/Instrument Blank" i=
njection.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">If this behavior is not d=
esired, rather than using the "No Injection/Instrument Blank" setting for I=
njection Source, continue to use the sampler or manual injector as the Inje=
ction Source, and instead use a 0 volume injection.  This will cause all si=
gnals, including the MBFC signals, to collect data.

If data has already been collected, the user may view the TIC Scan, TIC SIM=
, and/or extract individual SIMs or EICs in Data Analysis to view the colle=
cted MS data in the injection.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
