p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">A workflow issue has been=
 identified in OpenLAB CDS 2.2 and earlier versions that causes an upload e=
rror in the File Upload Queue, preventing pending files from being uploaded=
 to OpenLAB Server. The workflow described below is not recommended and sho=
uld be avoided.
1. Load a result set =E2=80=9CABC.rslt=E2=80=9D in Data Analysis
2. Open a processing method =E2=80=9CA.pmx=E2=80=9D from another result set=
 =E2=80=9CDEF.rslt=E2=80=9D
3. Link the processing method =E2=80=9CA.pmx=E2=80=9D with result set =E2=
=80=9CABC.rslt=E2=80=9D
4. Click on =E2=80=9CUpdate Master Method=E2=80=9D
5. Save all results
By doing above steps, the processing method =E2=80=9CA.pmx=E2=80=9D will ge=
t stuck in the File Upload Queue and causes error "Target file is inaccessi=
ble. Upload cannot be performed."</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Until the error is cleare=
d, all files in result set folder =E2=80=9CABC.rslt=E2=80=9D will stay in "=
Pending" status and waiting to be uploaded to the OpenLAB Server. Please co=
ntact Agilent Support for Service Note OpenLAB CDS-060 for details on how t=
o clear the error in File Upload Queue.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is resolved in=
 OpenLab CDS v2.3.</font></pre><p></p>




