<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">In some cases, the system=
 suitability results (e.g. the number of theoretical plates per column (USP=
) or resolution) cannot be reported in the software. To calculate those val=
ues the tangent width of a peak is needed. In case of high noise or high da=
ta rate of the chromatogram the correct determination of the tangent width =
will not be possible for some peaks. In such a case a calculation of the sy=
stem suitability values is not possible.</font></pre><p></p>
