roduces an advanced tangent calculation mode for noisy or high resolution s=
ignals. If this mode is activated the tangent construction is less sensitiv=
e with respect to noise.</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
<a id=3D"#TTID:" 232522=3D"" name=3D"TTID:232522"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:232522&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&nb=
sp;&nbsp;M8370AA&nbsp;&nbsp;2.3</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Data Analysis</fo=
nt></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Unable to integrate Child=
-Parent peak using EZChrom Integrator in OpenLab CDS 2.3</font></pre><p></p=
>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">When using the EZChrom in=
tegrator there is a check if the first time data point of the signal to be =
integrated starts at time zero.=20
If this is not the case one additional data point will be added to the sign=
al at time zero before the integration.=20
This is to allow EZChrom integrator to handle this specific situation.
Furthermore the EZChrom integrator can only work with equidistant data.=20
When we add an additional data point at time zero, even previously equidist=
ant data will become non-equidistant.=20
Therefore, the data needs to be re-sampled in a second step.=20
In Data Analysis we do this by spline interpolation.=20
The resampling slightly modifies the data, i.e. the data that is used for i=
ntegration is slightly different than the originally acquired data.
These slight modifications in the data introduced by the re-sampling is the=
 reason why the results differ in OpenLab CDS 2.3 from what the customer ge=
ts when using OpenLab CDS EZChrom.
</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Use the OpenLab CDS ChemS=
tation Integrator or perform a manual integration.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
