not be found in the content management. This can occur if a linked processi=
ng method got modified and the result set got reprocessed without saving th=
e modified processing method.=20
A preliminary version of the processing method will be tracked in the resul=
t set audit trail. If a new method gets linked afterwards to this result se=
t and saved after reprocessing, the result set audit trail will show an ent=
ry about the processing with the previously linked, modified, and unsaved p=
rocessing method.=20
Since the modified processing method was not saved, you will not find this =
version of the previously linked method in your content management.</font><=
/pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Save the changes of your =
linked processing method before you link a new method to the result set.</f=
ont></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is fixed in Op=
enLab CDS v2.7, and OpenLab CDS v2.6 Update 14.</font></pre><p></p>




