</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Toggling smoothing on and=
 off may result in compounds no longer linked to extracted signals</font></=
pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">When turning smoothing of=
f and on, it is possible to end up with compounds which are defined on EIC =
signals (target and/or qualifiers) which are no longer associated with any =
extracted EICs.  Results for these compounds can no longer be calculated un=
til the signal linkage is fixed, typically be deleting and readding the com=
pound and/or qualifier(s).</font></pre><p></p>
