</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Noise calculation on blan=
ks using extracted signals can be inconsistent</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">For result sets using ext=
racted signals for noise calculations, it is possible for sample results to=
 be calculated prior to the blanks being calculated, resulting in empty or =
incorrect noise (and signal to noise) results.  It is also possible for a b=
lank which is not the immediate prior blank in the result set to be used fo=
r the noise calculation.  And if the blank(s) are not linked to a method, o=
r are linked to a different method than the samples, it is possible to get =
an erroneous noise (and signal to noise) calculation.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">N/A</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is resolved in=
 OpenLab CDS v2.8 Update 08 with Feature Pack 02.</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
