<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:1204958&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CDS 2.7,CDS 3.0,CDS 2.8 Update 05</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Data Analysis</fo=
nt></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">TIC signals missing if sn=
apshot was taken during early time segment</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">For LCMS and GCMS data wh=
ich uses time segments in data acquisition: if a snapshot is taken during a=
n early time segment, and later time segments use different acquisition par=
ameters*, the TIC signals for the later time segments will not be visible i=
n CDS Data Analysis.  This issue will affect all subsequent injections in t=
he result set.

*The parameters which affect this include: polarity, gain, fragmentor volta=
ge, ionization mode (i.e. ESI or APCI on a Multimode source), and acquisiti=
on mode (i.e. SIM or Scan)</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Other than not taking a s=
napshot until the injection is into its final time segment, there is no kno=
wn workaround.  </font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">A fix for this issue will=
 be included in a future update.</font></pre><p></p>




