bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2.6 Update 14</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Data Analysis</fo=
nt></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Method inconsistency flag=
 after loading a result set where a master method was linked</font></pre><p=
></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">A user without the privil=
ege "Save Master Method" opened a master method and linked it to one inject=
ion of a result set before modifying the method. This created version 1 of =
the result set processing method.

Afterward, the modified processing method was linked to the rest of the inj=
ections, the result set was processed, and all was saved. This created vers=
ion 2 of the result set processing method.

Reopening this result set will show an inconsistency flag because obviously=
 version 1 of the result set method is linked.
</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Workaround:=20
After loading the result set and the master method, link it to all injectio=
ns before modifying the method. </font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This will be fixed in a f=
uture release</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
