<a id=3D"#TTID:" 401255=3D"" name=3D"TTID:401255"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:401255&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp=
;&nbsp;ECM XT v2.5</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Performance</font=
></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">SQL Server Database - 100=
% CPU Usage</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">On heavily used OpenLab S=
erver or ECM XT using Microsoft SQL Server 2014 or newer, the CPU can go to=
 100% making the system very slow and unusable.

With Microsoft SQL Server 2014, Microsoft introduced a new mechanism to pla=
n and execute queries and due to the new Cardinality Estimator (CE), certai=
n type of queries slows down due to plan regression.

Plan regression happens when SQL Server starts to use a sub-optimal plan to=
 execute a query. This behavior impacts the CPU (or Memory) resources of th=
e system.
 </font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">While the recommended wee=
kly maintenance plan  to update database statistics and rebuild indexes  wo=
rks for the majority of the OpenLab Server or ECM XT implementations, syste=
ms with many instruments and user sessions running concurrently or systems =
with high throughput instruments may need to increase the frequency of the =
=E2=80=9CUpdate Statistics=E2=80=9D maintenance plan to keep the SQL Server=
 statistics up to date such that the plan regression does not occur.=20
Queries involving the alf_prop_value and alf_prop_string_value tables will =
show plan regression as they are widely used by applications integrating wi=
th OpenLab Server or ECM XT such as OpenLab CDS Acquisition or OpenLab CDS =
Data Analysis.=20
=20
To bring back performance to normal
=20
1.       Review the currently implemented maintenance plan(s) on the SQL Se=
rver.=20
2.       Check if the maintenance plan(s) is/are set as per our recommendat=
ion and adjust as needed.
3.       Check when was the last time maintenance plan(s) got executed.=20
If the 100% CPU on the SQL Server continues to appear:
4.        Create an additional maintenance plan to update the statistics an=
d rebuild the index [optional] of the alf_prop_value and alf_prop_string_va=
lue tables=20
5.       Start with a twice a week schedule for the new plan and then to da=
ily as the load to the system increases.=20
Example(s):
A &gt; Weekly General Maintenance Plan scheduled to run on Sundays.
B &gt; Intermediate Maintenance plan for the alf_prop_value and alf_prop_st=
ring_value tables
=20
Day   S  M  T  W  T  F  S  S
Plan   A      B          B      A=20
=20
Day   S  M  T  W  T  F  S  S
Plan  A  B  B   B   B  B  B  A

The other solution is to upgrade to Microsoft SQL Server 2017 Enterprise Ed=
ition or Microsoft SQL Server 2019 Enterprise edition and enable the Automa=
tic Tuning feature.=20

Upgrading Microsoft SQL Server may require an upgrade of the OpenLab Server=
 or ECM XT application (see the Extra Information section for details)
In response to the performance degradation observed with Microsoft SQL Serv=
er 2014 and 2016, Microsoft introduced a new feature in Microsoft SQL Serve=
r 2017 called Automatic Tuning that addresses plan regression automatically=
. The Automatic Tuning feature is only available with the Enterprise Editio=
n.

To enable Automatic Tuning on Microsoft SQL Server 2017 Enterprise Edition =
or Microsoft SQL Server 2019 Enterprise edition, run the following 3 statem=
ents:
=20
DBCC FREEPROCCACHE=20

ALTER DATABASE [DataStore]
SET QUERY_STORE =3D ON
    (
      OPERATION_MODE =3D READ_WRITE,
      CLEANUP_POLICY =3D ( STALE_QUERY_THRESHOLD_DAYS =3D 90 ),
      DATA_FLUSH_INTERVAL_SECONDS =3D 900,
      QUERY_CAPTURE_MODE =3D AUTO,
      MAX_STORAGE_SIZE_MB =3D 1000,
      INTERVAL_LENGTH_MINUTES =3D 60,
      SIZE_BASED_CLEANUP_MODE =3D AUTO,
      MAX_PLANS_PER_QUERY =3D 200,
      WAIT_STATS_CAPTURE_MODE =3D ON
    );
ALTER DATABASE [DataStore]
SET AUTOMATIC_TUNING ( FORCE_LAST_GOOD_PLAN =3D ON );

 The weekly general maintenance as instructed in the OpenLab ECM XT Adminis=
tration guide is still needed to update statistics and check index fragment=
ation.

Additional Information:

OpenLab Server / SQL Server Compatibility=20

         2014  2016  2017  2019
v2.3      Y      Y
v2.4      Y      Y      Y
v2.5      Y      Y      Y       Y
=20
Microsoft Documentation: Additional Information on Database Statistics, Aut=
omatic Tuning and the Query Store database can be found at the following li=
nks:
=E2=80=A2	https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/automat=
ic-tuning/automatic-tuning?view=3Dsql-server-ver15
=E2=80=A2	https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/statist=
ics/statistics?view=3Dsql-server-ver15
=E2=80=A2	https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/sql/relational-databases/perform=
ance/best-practice-with-the-query-store?view=3Dsql-server-ver15
=20



=20
</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Upgrade SQL Server to 201=
7 Enterprise version and enable auto tuning</font></pre><p></p>




