<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:609704&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&nb=
sp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;2.6</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Performance</font=
></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Control Panel freezes whe=
n many users launch Acquisition and Data  Analysis at the same time in a cl=
ient server system.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">When many users are launc=
hing Acquisition and Data Analysis sessions=20
at once, the OpenLab Server / ECM XT Server performance can slow as=20
the requests are processed. The user experiences slow performance or=20
freezing of the Control Panel.=20

The underlying cause of this performance symptom is that the Apache=20
HTTPD employed by the Reverse Proxy server is configured by default to=20
support 64 ThreadsPerChild/Sessions. Because of this, high-traffic=20
Servers can slow-down or become unresponsive.=20

To verify whether this is the cause of a system=E2=80=99s poor performance,=
=20
review the error.log file located by default in C:\Program Files=20
(x86)\Agilent Technologies\OpenLab Reverse Proxy\Apache24\logs for=20
entries similar to those below:=20

[Thu Nov 18 23:24:45.624673 2021] [mpm_winnt:error] [pid 26544:tid=20
