<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:726704&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB&nbsp;&nbs=
p;Sample Scheduler&nbsp;&nbsp;2.5,2.6,2.7</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Performance</font=
></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Sample Scheduler Acquisit=
ion can get slower over the time with CDS 2.5, 2.6, 2.7</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Sample Scheduler uses the=
 CDS Acquisition API which gets slower over the time depending on the numbe=
r of connections made over the API. With a new connection to the instrument=
, a user change, or change of the CDS project, another registry entry gets =
written by the Diagnostics Dashboard under HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\WOW6=
432Node\Agilent\Diagnostics. With the growing amount of registry entries, t=
he Acquisition API may get remarkable slower, depending on the overall syst=
em performance.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Excessive registry entrie=
s created by the Acquisition API can be cleaned up by running following Pow=
erShell script with Administrator privileges:

$agenteCount =3D (get-process Agilent.OpenLAB.Acquisition.AcquisitionAgente=
* | measure-object).count
if ($agenteCount)
{
     Write-Host "Please first close your $agenteCount Agilent.OpenLAB.Acqui=
sition.AcquisitionAgente process(es)"
     exit;
}
gci -path HKLM:\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\Agilent\Diagnostics\ | %{get-itemprope=
rty -path $_.pspath} | ?{$_.application.Contains("AcquisitionAgente-")} | %=
{"Cleaning $($_.pspath)";remove-item -path $_.pspath }</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">The problem will not occu=
r in CDS 2.8 due to a change in the architecture. Fixes are planned in Upda=
tes for CDS 2.5, 2.6 and 2.7. </font></pre><p></p>




