MQ\log and restart the service. The rabbitmq service can also be configured=
 to rotate the logfile daily and keep 5 days worth of logs by editing C:\Pr=
ogramData\Agilent\OpenLab Platform\RabbitMQ\rabbitmq.conf to have the follo=
wing settings:

log.file =3D C:\ProgramData\Agilent\LogFiles\OpenLab Platform\RabbitMQ\rabb=
itmq.log
# keep up to 5 archived log files in addition to the current one
log.file.rotation.count =3D 5
##  $D0 -&gt; rotate a log file every 24 hours at midnight
log.file.rotation.date =3D $D0

</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>




