=3DSequence_Description =3D "SST01"

If the sequence description does not contain anything, the report generatio=
n will fail, and no report will be generated.

This is a known issue of OpenLAB CDS 2.1 and will be fixed in OpenLAB CDS 2=
.2.=20
The report template will remain functional if the sequence description cont=
ains a value.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Change the corresponding =
expressions using conversion functions:
" =3DCStr(Sequence_Description) =3D "SST01" "=20

Conversion functions are recommended to evaluate the result of an expected =
value with the value captured during the analysis.

Examples:
CSt() converts any type of value to string
Val() converts any type of values to double</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is fixed in Op=
enLAB CDS v2.2.
</font></pre><p></p>




