</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Installation fails at the=
 reverse proxy step due to port 5443 being used by another program</font></=
pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">In OpenLab CDS 2.6, port =
5443 needs to be available at time of deployment for reverse proxy installa=
tion. </font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Disable the program that =
uses port 5443 at the time of deployment.  At the Step 4 installation step,=
 the proxy is reconfigured and removes this dependency making port 5443 ava=
ilable for another program.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is fixed in Op=
enLab CDS v2.7.</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
<a id=3D"#TTID:" 670922=3D"" name=3D"TTID:670922"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:670922&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&nb=
sp;&nbsp;Installer&nbsp;&nbsp;CDS 2.7</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Workflow</font></=
p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">System preparation someti=
mes hangs at the Tcp Port Sharing and Activation step</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">During System Preparation=
, the Tcp Port Sharing and Activation remains in a running status without c=
ompleting. </font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Cancel the system prepara=
tion step and re-start the installation. A message is shown to reboot the m=
achine. After rebooting and restarting the installation, it completes. </fo=
nt></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue got resolved i=
n OpenLab CDS v2.8.</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
<a id=3D"#TTID:" 1217114=3D"" name=3D"TTID:1217114"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:1217114&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CDS 2.8,ECM XT 2.8</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Workflow</font></=
p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Test Services - Workflow =
test goes into a pending status</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">When upgrading from a leg=
acy CDS version to OpenLab 2.8, the CDS Workflow Test on an AIC might stay =
at pending status and it will not progress. Issue is related to a product n=
ame change in the newer versions of the OpenLab CDS.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">n/a</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is fixed in Ag=
ilent Test Services 3.6 Patch 03, OpenLab Server v2.8 Update 08, and OpenLa=
b CDS v2.8 Update 08 with Feature Pack 02.</font></pre><p></p>




<hr>
<a id=3D"#TTID:" 1289465=3D"" name=3D"TTID:1289465"></a>
<b><font color=3D"#3399FF">KPR#:1289465&nbsp;&nbsp;Product:OpenLAB - CDS2&n=
bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CDS 2.7</font></b><br>
<p><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Keyword:&nbsp;Workflow</font></=
p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">One-line Description:</font>=
</b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">OpenLab storage system te=
st fails with ECM 3.6.7 backend</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Problem:</font></b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">Due to changes introduced=
 with ECM 3.6 Update 07, the storage system test fails when OpenLab 2.7 is =
configured with ECM 3.6.7 as the storage backend.</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Temporary Solution:</font></=
b><br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">None</font></pre><p></p>
<p><b><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"3">Fix Information:</font></b><=
br>
</p><pre><font face=3D"arial,sanserif" size=3D"2">This issue is fixed in Op=
enLab CDS 2.8 Update 08 with Feature Pack 02. For OpenLab CDS 2.7 there is =
no fix.</font></pre><p></p>


